              "text": "occō, occāre — \"to harrow, to break up the soil\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Agricola agrum prīmum arat, deinde occat. The farmer first ploughs the field, then harrows it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "occō, occāre, occāvī, occātum, from occa 'a harrow'."
            }
          ]
        },
