          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "occō is built on occa 'a harrow' (EtymDB), from the PIE root h₂eḱ- 'sharp'. Lewis & Short give German eggen 'to harrow' as a cousin."
            }
          ]
        },
